================================
electrochemistry-data Change Log
================================

.. current developments

v0.10.0
====================

**Added:**

* Added DOIs to all entries in ``literature/bibliography/bibliography.bib`` that have one, taken from ``source.url`` of the corresponding YAML files, so that the ``bibdata`` shipped with each datapackage includes a persistent identifier (#179).
* Added ``pixi run -e dev validate-bib-dois`` (part of ``validate-input`` and ``validate-new-input``), which checks that the ``doi`` of each bibliography entry is a bare DOI and agrees with ``source.url`` of every entry citing it.
* Added ``validate-citation-keys`` to ``validate-input``, checking that every
  ``citationKey`` resolves to a bibliography entry.
* Added ``CONTRIBUTING.md`` that distinguishes data contributions (adding, checking and correcting entries, no programming required) from technical contributions (tooling, CI, review assistants), with a step-by-step guide for adding digitized figures and source data, the expected level of detail of the metadata, rules and standard phrases for curator comments, local checks, the review and release process, and how to report errors in existing entries. (#180)
* Added issue templates for errors in existing entries and for questions about data submissions.
* Added the ``check-news`` pixi task and a CI workflow that checks that every pull request adds a well-formed news entry.
* Added the working electrode area reported in the publication to ``atkin_2011_situ_6849``, ``atkin_2014_structure_44``, ``borisenko_2006_situ_6250``, ``borisenko_2012_situ_1736``, ``gasparotto_2009_situ_11140`` (``0.3 cm2``) and ``jovic_1999_cyclic_247`` (``0.316 cm2``). Areas defined by an O-ring are marked with ``effectiveElectrodeSurfaceArea`` in the quantity comment.
* Added the working electrode area of ``alves_2011_electrochemistry_6010`` (``0.283 cm2``), calculated from the 6 mm O-ring of the flow cell.
* Added electrode diameters reported in the publications to ``abe_2019_electro-oxidation_315``, ``abou_2003_electrosorption_211``, ``clavilier_1980_preparation_205``, ``ganassin_2015_non-covalent_8349``, ``meng_2012_hydrogen_5222``, ``wandlowski_1996_structural_10277`` and ``wang_1996_ordered_6672``.
* Added comments on the origin of the electrode area or diameter to ``friedl_2017_interface_216``, ``hermann_2021_effect_138279``, ``schonig_2023_entropic_5948`` and ``tiwari_2020_fingerprint_1450``.
* Added a checklist for updating the metadata-schema version to ``CONTRIBUTING.md``, and the rule that news entries for bulk changes describe what changed instead of listing the affected entries.
* Added a check to ``validate-input`` that every input YAML declares ``echemdbSchemaVersion`` equal to the current schema version.

**Changed:**

* Changed the ``doi`` of ``sato_2006_effect_725`` from a URL to a bare DOI and removed the redundant ``url`` field of ``blizanac_2004_anion_625``.
* Changed the ``data`` and ``Test`` CI workflows to trigger via
  ``paths-ignore`` instead of an allowlist, so that changes outside the
  data/documentation fast-path (e.g. workflows, ``util/``, ``pixi.lock``, root
  config) now run the full checks. Pure-documentation PRs are still skipped;
  ``Test`` additionally skips pure-data PRs.
* Changed the ``Validate Examples`` CI workflow to run ``validate-input`` on
  every PR.
* Changed the curator comments (`figureDescription.comment`) of digitized entries to consistent full sentences that only describe the data and how it was traced, e.g., a unified phrase for curator-estimated zero-current baselines and fixed typos.
* Changed the pull request template to a short checklist that links to ``CONTRIBUTING.md``.
* Changed the contributing section of the README to link to ``CONTRIBUTING.md``.
* Changed metadata-schema version from 0.8.3 to 0.9.0.
* Changed ``migrate-metadata`` to set ``echemdbSchemaVersion`` in all input YAML files, editing only the stamp line in files without structural changes.
* Changed svgdigitizer dependency from 0.14.5 to 0.15.0, which records the name and version of svgdigitizer as ``figureDescription.software`` in the generated data packages.

**Removed:**

* Removed the ``Quick Data Check`` CI workflow, which is covered by
  ``Validate Examples``.
* Removed curator comments that do not describe the traced data (scientific context, details already contained in the metadata such as the reference electrode or techniques, missing counter electrode information) from `abou_2003_electrosorption_211`, `gomez-marin_2012_pt-111_558`, `kerner_2002_measurement_2055` (f2a), `lipkowski_1998_ionic_2875`, and `wallauer_2013_differential_1143`.
* Removed the template placeholder comment from the source data of `engstfeld_2018_polycrystalline_17743`.
* Removed support for Python 3.10, which reached its end of life in October 2026. The database tooling now requires Python 3.11 or later.
* Removed the workaround for UTF-8 characters outside latin-1 in ``validate-bib-keys``, which svgdigitizer 0.15.0 handles itself.

**Fixed:**

* Fixed ``validate-new-input`` skipping renamed entries and, for changes
  without a changed entry (e.g. bibliography only), the bibliography checks.
* Fixed invalid ``geometricElectrolyteContactArea`` of the working electrode in 43 entries (#181). The key is removed where the publication does not report an area; the electrode diameter from the publication is recorded in ``shape.diameter`` instead (``briega-martos_2020_hydrogen_135452``, ``briega-martos_2021_cation_48``, ``chen_2024_deconvolution_4958``, ``cuesta_2000_adsorption_5684``, ``engstfeld_2018_polycrystalline_17743``, ``sato_2006_effect_725``).
* Fixed the working electrode area of ``jerkiewicz_2009_effect_12309`` (``0.0431 cm2`` instead of ``4.31 1 / mm2``) and the electrode diameter, using the values and uncertainties reported in the publication.
* Fixed the electrode diameter of ``engstfeld_2018_polycrystalline_17743`` (6 mm sample in the hanging meniscus cell, 8 mm sample in the flow cell) and described how the electrolyte contact area is defined in each cell.
* Fixed ``durand_1992_situ_1977``: added the working electrode area (``1.12 cm2``) and dimensions, corrected the crystallographic orientation (``100`` instead of ``110``), the reference electrode (SCE instead of RHE), and the swapped value and unit of the Ar pressure.
* Fixed empty ``shape.height`` entries without a value in ``briega-martos_2020_hydrogen_135452``, ``briega-martos_2021_cation_48`` and ``chen_2024_deconvolution_4958``.
* Fixed the working electrode of ``howlett_2006_electrochemistry_1483``: removed the area of ``1 cm2``, which the publication does not report.
* Fixed the working electrode type of the Au(111) films on mica (``atkin_2009_afm_13266``, ``atkin_2011_situ_6849``, ``atkin_2014_structure_44``, ``borisenko_2006_situ_6250``, ``borisenko_2012_situ_1736``, ``endres_2006_probing_1377``, ``gasparotto_2009_situ_11140``) from ``single crystal`` to ``highly oriented thin film``.
* Fixed ``blizanac_2004_anion_625`` by removing the electrode diameter, which was derived from the area and not reported in the publication.



v0.9.2
====================

**Added:**

* Added a regression doctest for ``validate_bib_keys`` covering bibliography entries with UTF-8 characters outside latin-1 (e.g. ``Jović``), guarding the hotfix for `svgdigitizer#300 <https://github.com/echemdb/svgdigitizer/issues/300>`_.

**Fixed:**

* Fixed several inconsistent unit names.



v0.9.1
====================

**Added:**

* Added a scheduled GitHub Actions workflow (``check-metadata-schema.yml``)
  that checks weekly for new ``echemdb/metadata-schema`` releases and opens a
  pull request bumping ``SCHEMA_VERSION`` in ``echemdb_ecdata/validate.py``
  when a newer version is available. The run is idempotent (it skips when an
  update branch or PR already exists) and uses an optional
  ``METADATA_SCHEMA_PAT`` secret so the generated PR triggers CI, falling back
  to ``GITHUB_TOKEN`` when the secret is not configured.
* Added figures 1-3 from Droog and Schlenter, 1980 (oxygen electrosorption on Cu(111), Cu(110), Cu(100) single crystals in 1 mol/l NaOH).
* Added supporting-information figure S2 (A, B, C) from Huang et al., 2017 (cyclic voltammograms of Cu(100), Cu(111), Cu(110) single crystals in N2-purged 0.1 M KOH).
* Added digitized data and bibliography entry for ``jovic_2002_surface_531``.
  Figures 1a (Cu(111)) and 1b (Cu(100)): cyclic voltammograms recorded in
  0.1 M NaOH at a sweep rate of 100 mV/s, with potentials referenced vs SHE
  (Hg/HgO-0.1M-NaOH reference electrode).
* Added digitized data and bibliography entry for ``kunze_2003_situ_113``.
  Figures 1a and 1b: cyclic voltammograms of a Cu(001) single crystal
  recorded in 0.1 M NaOH at a sweep rate of 20 mV/s, with potentials
  referenced vs SHE.
* Added digitized data and bibliography entry for ``le_2017_role_13099``.
  Figure S5a: cyclic voltammogram of a Cu(100) single crystal recorded in
  0.1 M NaOH.
* Added figure 1 (base cyclic voltammograms of Pt(111), Pt(100), Pt(110) in
  0.1 M KOH) from Markovic et al., 1996.
* Added PR review skills, which can be used by both Claude and Copilot using for digitized data `review-literature-pr <foldername>` or for source data `review-source-data-pr <foldername>`
* Added digitized data for schouten_2013_electrochemical_6 (Schouten et al., 2013):
  blank cyclic voltammograms of five Cu single crystals (Cu(111), Cu(100),
  Cu(110), Cu(322), Cu(911)) in 0.1 M NaOH from figure 1.
* Added a ``convert-svg-one`` pixi task to convert and validate a single
  svgdigitizer paper folder, for quick local checks without rebuilding all
  entries. Usage: ``pixi run -e dev convert-svg-one <paper>``.
* Added raw CV data (CNad-free Pt(111)) for figures 1a, 2a and 2c from
  Strmcnik et al., Nature Chemistry 2, 880 (2010).
* Added ``mdstools`` (the tooling shipped with the
  `metadata-schema repository <https://github.com/echemdb/metadata-schema>`_,
  pinned to the release matching ``echemdb_ecdata.validate.SCHEMA_VERSION``)
  as a dev-environment dependency.
* Added ``migrate-metadata`` and ``migrate-metadata-dry-run`` tasks
  (``echemdb_ecdata.migrate``) that upgrade the input YAML metadata in
  ``literature/`` across breaking metadata-schema releases using the
  migration engine of the metadata-schema repository. Rewritten files are
  stamped with ``echemdbSchemaVersion``.
* Added digitized data and bibliography entry for ``wang_2001_situ_2809``.
  Figure 2: cyclic voltammograms of a Ru(0001) single-crystal working electrode
  (hanging meniscus, 10 mV/s) in 1 M HClO4 (2a), 0.1 M HClO4 (2b), and an
  alkaline pH 14 solution (2c, solid and dashed sweeps).
* Added support for authoring the Zenodo release description in a separate
  Markdown file (``zenodo-description.md``) via the ``--description`` option of
  ``zenodo-publish``. Markdown is rendered to HTML at publish time, so the
  description no longer has to be maintained as an escaped JSON string in
  ``zenodo.json``.
* Added CC-BY-4.0 and ODC-By-1.0 data-license badges to the README.
* Added a direct download link to the latest release ZIP and a note on
  downloading the archive from Zenodo to the README "Accessing Data" section.
  The release link's version is bumped automatically via ``rever.xsh``.
* Added documentation to the README that data can also be submitted directly as
  raw CSV files (under ``literature/source_data/``), in addition to data
  digitized from publications with ``svgdigitizer``.

**Changed:**

* Changed lower bound of svgdigitizer to 0.14.4.
* Changed lower bound of `svgdigitizer` to v0.14.5.
* Changed metadata-schema version (``mdstools`` git tag and ``SCHEMA_VERSION``) from 0.8.2 to 0.8.3 and flipped the ``click`` pin from ``<8.2`` to ``>=8.2`` (required by ``linkml`` 1.11.1, on which ``mdstools`` 0.8.3 depends).
* Changed the metadata-schema version to 0.8.2 and migrated all input YAML
  files accordingly: ``system.electrolyte.temperature`` moved to
  ``experimental.operationParameters.temperature``.
* Changed schema validation to use the validation tools of the
  metadata-schema repository (``mdstools``) instead of ``check-jsonschema``:
  the JSON Schema is fetched once per run and all files are validated
  in-process, now also including the instrument-reference check for
  ``experimental.operationParameters`` control blocks.
* Changed the ``--version`` argument of the validation tasks to take a plain
  metadata-schema release tag (e.g. ``0.8.0``) or branch name (e.g. ``main``)
  instead of ``tags/X.Y.Z`` / ``head/branch-name``.
* Changed the ``data/Makefile`` license and directory-creation recipes to use
  Python instead of the ``cp``/``mkdir`` Unix utilities so they also work on
  Windows.

**Removed:**

* Removed the ``check-jsonschema`` dependency.

**Fixed:**

* Fixed ``.gitignore`` so generated CSVs in ``literature/svgdigitizer`` subfolders are ignored (previously only matched files directly in ``literature/svgdigitizer/``).
* Fixed ``validate-bib-keys`` crashing with ``UnicodeEncodeError`` on bibliography entries containing UTF-8 characters outside latin-1 (e.g. ``Jović``, ``Adžić``), by escaping such characters as LaTeX sequences before passing them to ``svgdigitizer.pdf.Pdf.build_identifier`` (hotfix for `svgdigitizer#300 <https://github.com/echemdb/svgdigitizer/issues/300>`_).
* Fixed the generated data archive (and thus the release zip and Zenodo upload)
  not containing the license files. The ``convert`` task now copies
  ``LICENSE.md``, ``LICENSE-GPL-3.0-or-later``, ``LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0`` and
  ``LICENSE-ODC-By-1.0`` into ``data/generated``.



